{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839775-how-to-convert-1st-ed-s-already-made-characters-in-second-edition","id":839775,"title":"How to convert 1st ed's already-made characters in second edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T03:17:11-08:00","id":839775,"title":"How to convert 1st ed's already-made characters in second edition?","content":"I mean, how to convert the Shadow Gifts? For vampires and mages it's easy - altough effects were changed, Celerity 2 or Prime 3 will be still Celerity 2 or Prime 3. But for werewolves this work only for Moon gifts, while others were changed very much. For example, this is the gift set of sample character from Lodges-The Faithful;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gifts: (1) Clarity, Feet of Mist, Know Name, Mask of Rage,<br /> Sense Malice, Ward Versus Predators, Wolf-Blood\u2019s Lure;<br /> (2) Attunement, Father Wolf\u2019s Speed, Hone Rage, Scent of<br /> Taint, Traveler\u2019s Blessing, Ward Versus Humans; (3) Death<br /> Grip, Leach Rage, Primal Howl, True Leader, Sagacity; (4)<br /> Savage Rending, Rage Armor, Rekindled Rage<br /> Rituals: 3; Rites: (1) Banish Human, Funeral Rite, Rite of<br /> Dedication, Rite of the Ghost Howl, Rite of the Spirit Brand;<br /> (2) Banish Spirit, Fortify the Border Marches; (3) Bind Human,<br /> Bind Spirit, Rite of Contrition, Rite of Healing </div> </div> </div>Except of Auspice gift and rituals, I don't know, how much gifts this guy should have in CotD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T03:56:54-08:00","id":839783,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, look at the character's auspice Renown and give that many levels of 2e Moon Gifts. Remove any 1e auspice Gifts from the list. See how many other Gifts the character has and replace it with a similar number of 2e Facets - maybe trade two 1e level 1 or 2 gifts for a facet, swap level 3 in a straight exchange, and give 2 facets for level 4 or 5 Gifts. Choose Gifts/Facets that are appropriate to the character's Renown and the 1e Gifts they had. Add or subtract a few Facets until it feels about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T06:19:10-08:00","id":839847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839775-how-to-convert-1st-ed-s-already-made-characters-in-second-edition#post839775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, how to convert the Shadow Gifts? For vampires and mages it's easy - altough effects were changed, Celerity 2 or Prime 3 will be still Celerity 2 or Prime 3. But for werewolves this work only for Moon gifts, while others were changed very much. For example, this is the gift set of sample character from Lodges-The Faithful;<br /> <br /> Except of Auspice gift and rituals, I don't know, how much gifts this guy should have in CotD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are Full Moon, Stealth, Knowledge, Rage, Insight, Warding and Father Wolf Gifts. You just give him appropriate facets from the second edition Gifts. For Father Wolf you should substitute Wolf Gifts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}